# Secrets and local-only files. The CI secret scan (gitleaks) enforces this
# in every run, but .gitignore is the first line of defence: a secret that
# is never committed cannot leak from the repo. Never add a token, key,
# or password here — or anywhere in this repo.
.env*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.token
*-token.txt
credentials*
*secret*
# Wrangler / Node local state
.wrangler/
node_modules/
# Generated in CI, never committed (stale copies would lie about what is live)
public/version.json
# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
*.log
